## End-to-end exercise of `Class.static_method(args).await` —
## the class-static-method-call awaitee shape in `describe_await`
## (`async_lowering/mod.rs`). Unblocks the deferred slice from
## task #21.
##
## What changed to unblock this: `lower_async_defs` now walks
## bootstrap stdlib programs when populating its awaitee tables
## (`collect_class_static_returns_into` /
## `collect_future_outputs_into`). `Async` and `TimeSleepFuture`
## live in library/std/future/src/lib.rx, invisible to the
## previous user-program-only walks. See
## `project_ruxen_async_compiler_gaps.md` (#2).
##
## Shape:
##   async def doit() -> nil
##     let _ = Async.sleep(Duration.from_millis(50)).await
##     ()
##   end
##
## The `.await` desugar treats `Async.sleep(d)` as an awaitee whose
## Future class is `TimeSleepFuture` (declared in
## library/std/future/src/lib.rx) and whose Output is `()` (read from
## the future's `poll(...) -> Poll[nil]` method signature). The synth
## state machine has:
##   __state: Int
##   __sub_0: TimeSleepFuture   # constructed via `Async.sleep(...)` directly
##   sleep_done: nil             # hoisted from the .await binding
##
## NOTE on binding shape: the await-let binding uses a named
## identifier (`sleep_done`), not `_` — the AST async-lowering
## segmenter currently requires `Pattern::Identifier` for the
## await-let target. Wildcard support (`let _ = X.await`) is a
## separate slice (memory: "async-lowering let _ shape").
##
## Runtime sequence mirrors fixture 725 (block_on directly on
## Async.sleep) — first poll registers a timer + returns Pending, the
## block_on parks on Thread.yield_now -> reactor wait, the timer fires,
## next poll returns Ready, the outer state machine resolves.
##
## Tolerance window 40-200ms matches fixture 725 / 555.

use std.time.Instant
use std.time.Duration

async def doit() -> nil
  let sleep_done = Async.sleep(Duration.from_millis(50)).await
  sleep_done
end

def main
  let start = Instant.now()
  block_on(doit())
  let elapsed = start.elapsed()
  let nanos = elapsed.as_nanos()
  if nanos >= 40000000 && nanos <= 200000000
    puts "ok"
  else
    puts "fail"
  end
end
